          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.407,
            0.1,
            0.591,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SUMMARY"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.134,
            0.822,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When two lines intersect, they form four angles. The vertically opposite angles are equal and the linear pairs add up to 180°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.173,
            0.823,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When two lines intersect and the angles formed are 90° (i.e., all four angles are equal), the lines are said to be perpendicular to each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.212,
            0.822,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When two lines never intersect on a plane, they are called parallel lines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.249,
            0.823,
            0.306
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When a line t intersects another pair of lines, it is called a transversal and it forms 2 sets of 4 angles. Each of the 4 angles in the first set has a corresponding angle in the second set."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.307,
            0.823,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When a transversal intersects a pair of parallel lines, the corresponding angles are equal. When a transversal intersects a pair of lines and the corresponding angles are equal, then the pair of lines is parallel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.383,
            0.822,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When a transversal intersects a pair of parallel lines, the alternate angles are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.421,
            0.822,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The interior angles on the same side formed by a transversal intersecting a pair of parallel lines always add up to 180°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
